  "answer": "When adding 3.75 and 2.6, we align the decimal points and add the numbers column by column. 3.75 has 3 units, 7 tenths, and 5 hundredths. 2.6 has 2 units and 6 tenths. Adding these, we get 5 units, 13 tenths (which is 1 unit and 3 tenths), and 5 hundredths. This results in 6 units, 3 tenths, and 5 hundredths, or 6.35.",
