  "answer": "When the ball is dropped from a height, it starts with potential energy due to its position. As it falls, this potential energy converts into kinetic energy. When the ball hits the ground, some of the kinetic energy is converted into thermal energy and sound energy. As the ball bounces back up, the remaining kinetic energy converts back into potential energy. The different types of energy involved are potential energy, kinetic energy, thermal energy, and sound energy. The detailed description of the energy changes shows how energy is conserved and transformed throughout the process.",
  "reasoning": "The question requires students to explain the energy transformations and identify the types of energy involved at each stage, which aligns with the target cognitive demand of Bloom's level 'Understand' and DOK level 'DOK4'. The detailed description of the energy changes encourages deeper analysis and reasoning."
