['{
  "question": "A rectangular coil of wire is moved perpendicularly through a uniform magnetic field directed into the page. Using Lenz's Law, explain the direction of the induced current in the coil as it enters and exits the magnetic field.",
  "answer": "As the coil enters the magnetic field, the magnetic flux through the coil increases. According to Lenz's Law, the induced current will oppose this change by creating a magnetic field directed out of the page. This results in a counterclockwise current when viewed from above. As the coil exits the magnetic field, the magnetic flux decreases, so the induced current creates a magnetic field into the page, resulting in a clockwise current when viewed from above.",
  "reasoning": "The question requires students to analyze the scenario using Lenz's Law to determine the direction of the induced current, which involves understanding the change in magnetic flux and applying the law to predict the induced current direction. This matches the Analyze level in Bloom's taxonomy and DOK3, as it requires students to break down the scenario into parts and understand the relationships between the variables."
