bocation intermediate. The SN1 mechanism generally has a lower yield and selectivity due to the formation of carbocation intermediates that can undergo elimination or rearrangement, while the SN2 mechanism offers higher yield and selectivity due to its concerted nature. To maximize the yield of the desired product, one should use a polar aprotic solvent and control the temperature to minimize side reactions. The limitations of the SN1 mechanism include the formation of carbocation intermediates that can undergo elimination or rearrangement, leading to side products. The SN2 mechanism is limited by steric hindrance, which can slow down the reaction. To overcome these limitations, one could use a more sterically unhindered substrate for the SN2 mechanism or modify the solvent to stabilize the carbocation intermediate in the SN1 mechanism. To test the effect of solvent polarity on the reaction rate and stereochemical outcome, one could conduct a series of experiments using different solvents with varying polarities and measure the reaction rate and stereochemical outcome of the SN1 and SN2 mechanisms. This would involve preparing the same reactants in different solvents, monitoring the reaction progress, and analyzing the products using techniques such as NMR or GC-MS. The experimental design could be improved by using a controlled environment, ensuring consistent reaction conditions, and employing multiple trials to ensure reliability and accuracy of the results. A new synthetic route to achieve the same product with higher yield and selectivity could involve using a different nucleophile or a different substrate that is less prone to side reactions, such as using a primary alkyl halide in a polar aprotic solvent to favor the SN2 mechanism.", "reasoning": "The question requires students to analyze and compare two reaction mechanisms (SN1 and SN2), evaluate their effectiveness, and propose strategies to improve synthetic outcomes. It also involves designing an experiment and critically evaluating its design, which aligns with the Analyze level and DOK4 cognitive demand."}']

