  "question": "Design a laboratory experiment to demonstrate the effect of temperature on the equilibrium position of the reaction: N\u2082(g) + 3H\u2082(g) \u21cc 2NH\u2083(g). Include the materials needed, procedure, and expected observations.",
  "answer": "Materials: A sealed container with a pressure gauge, nitrogen gas, hydrogen gas, a heating source, a cooling source, and a thermometer.\nProcedure: 1. Fill the container with a known amount of nitrogen and hydrogen gases at a specific temperature and pressure. 2. Measure the initial pressure and temperature. 3. Heat the container to a higher temperature and observe the change in pressure. 4. Cool the container to a lower temperature and observe the change in pressure. 5. Record the pressure and temperature at each step.\nExpected observations: When the temperature is increased, the pressure will decrease, indicating a shift in equilibrium towards the reactants (N\u2082 and H\u2082). When the temperature is decreased, the pressure will increase, indicating a shift in equilibrium towards the products (NH\u2083).",
